1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,151
A sensor in a field runs on a battery. If it stays wide awake all day, the battery

2
00:00:06,151 --> 00:00:07,460
drains. So it naps.

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:12,906
The alarm clock is a low power timer. The one who shakes you awake is the wake-up

4
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:13,180
unit.

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:19,037
The bed is a deep sleep called low leakage stop. Memory is kept, so the program

6
00:00:19,037 --> 00:00:20,800
continues where it paused.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:27,400
Fast clocks switch off in deep sleep. Our alarm uses a slow clock that ticks one

8
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,200
thousand times a second and keeps going.

9
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,540
How many ticks for five seconds?

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:38,040
Your turn. Pause the video.

11
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,080
Five thousand.

12
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:45,600
Deep sleep is locked by default, for safety. The program must unlock it first.

13
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:54,360
Sleep five seconds. Wake. Blink. Read tilt and light. Send. Sleep again.

14
00:00:55,360 --> 00:01:00,400
A Bluetooth module called HC-05 turns serial text into radio.

15
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:07,460
Our message is simple: X, Y, Z and light, separated by commas, at 9600 speed.

16
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:13,481
One device's send wire goes to the other's receive wire. Like two people: one's

17
00:01:13,481 --> 00:01:15,260
mouth faces the other's ear.

